 "conclusions": [
  "Offline model and live Core agree for the default (auto) cell: 43-44 of 51 offline; live 43 (session count, STT ok) and 43 (detections, STT crashed). Conditioning off: offline 43-45; live detections 44 and 39. Zero false triggers on the 54 negatives in every valid live run, and on 66 min of real noise in every offline cell.",
  "Warm-up 3 s matters: without it offline hits spread 36-47 across repeats; with it 43-44.",
  "Conditioning auto removes the babble false trigger that conditioning off produced in one offline repeat (default, warm-up 3 s, repeat 0; in the packaged cell it did not fire). It costs no hits.",
  "Boost 1.2 with phrase threshold 0.22 is the highest-hit setting with zero false triggers; boost 1.4 or 1.6 admits the 10 s babble clip in 1 of 6 repeats; thresholds 0.15 to 0.22 change nothing; 0.26 loses one hit on average.",
  "Hit variance between runs comes from clip alignment on the stream: borderline positives change outcome with a sub-chunk shift of the same clip (placement sweep), not from rotation phase or the threshold.",
  "The earlier live runs at 37/51 (A13) and 41-50 (A7) used session-based counts; with STT failing or restarting, sessions can be missed. The detection-based counts above are the measure of the wake path.",
  "STT worker crashed (worker_crashed), restarted, and was marked failed in all three detection-era live runs. Wake detection kept working; sessions after the failure ended as stt_failed. Cause not found in this round."
